# RESOLVED 2026-08-09: 7fbc7bc9 (#1598) restored. _greedy_argmax_step ->
# _fused_greedy_step, now calling the model's fused_greedy_decode. The commit was
# HALF-landed: models/qwen3_5/language.py already had fused_greedy_decode,
# supports_fused_greedy_logits_processors and _can_target_verify_quantized_head,
# so the model exposed the fast quantized-argmax path and NOTHING CALLED IT --
# the optimization was inert. Taking upstream's current _fused_greedy_step also
# lands 6d5603b3 (#1628)'s second half, which b616f889 skipped for want of this
# very method, and ea2edd68 (#1583)'s _ensure_logits_processor_slots.
#
# CORRECTION 2026-08-09 (later, while draining the fork-marker allowlist): "restored"
# above was one half short, and this note is why nobody looked again. 7fbc7bc9 did not
# merely ADD _can_target_verify_quantized_head -- it EXTRACTED it out of
# _can_target_verify_quantized and rewrote that function to call it. Only the
# extraction landed, so this tree kept the pre-split body and carried the same
# predicate twice, one copy of which no longer had a caller-side reason to exist. That
# is trap 6 in the handoff ("a partially-restored commit is unfinished") applied to a
# commit already recorded as finished: the note named THREE symbols it had verified
# present and treated their presence as the commit being whole, when what was missing
# was a rewrite of a FOURTH symbol that was present all along. Presence of a symbol
# says nothing about whether its body is upstream's. Now converged, and guarded by
# tests/test_dropped_upstream_guards.py::TestQwen35QuantizedVerifyPredicateIsFactored.

