# --- mlx_vlm/server/generation.py
# RESOLVED 2026-08-10: 29b6c00b (#1508) restored, and _generate_masked_diffusion plus
# its nested flush/on_block DELETED as stale. The conclusive test from AGENTS.md:
# our copy differed from upstream's last pre-deletion copy in exactly two spots, both
# the `args.skip_special_tokens` -> `True` regression that f044f36a (#1359) had left
# behind — so the fork never authored this function. STALE, not FORK.
#
# The commit had landed in six of its eleven files, which is what hid it:
# generate/diffusion.py is byte-identical to upstream, so the unified engine and
# stream_diffusion_generate_from_kwargs were present and even called from
# generate/dispatch.py. Only the SERVER call site was dropped, and
# check_dead_helpers.py is blind to that because the helper does have a caller.
# The app.py half had also landed — relocated into server/request_normalization.py by
# 221fe0b3 (#1644) and restored with the gen-args union, which is why the 13 request
# knobs reached GenerationArguments correctly and looked fine in isolation.
#
# What made it a live bug rather than dead code: the fork kept `_run_diffusion(family)`
# selecting `_generate_diffusion` only when `family == "block"`, but
# `diffusion_generation_family` is upstream's backward-compatible shim and returns only
# "diffusion" or None. So the unified path was UNREACHABLE and every diffusion request
# fell through to the stale one, which read no request knobs at all. Consequences, none
# with a failing test:
#   * All 13 diffusion request options (block_length, max_denoising_steps, threshold,
#     diffusion_sampler, ...) were silently ignored at serving time; the stale path took
#     its sampler tuning from `config.default_diffusion_*` only.
#   * `skip_special_tokens` and `top_k` were ignored — f044f36a's dropped generation.py
#     half, live on the only reachable path.
#   * Structured response_format raised ValueError instead of being forwarded.
#   * Streaming chunks never carried `generation_tps`; StreamingToken has the field, so
#     diffusion responses just always reported a null decode rate.
# The fork's own test called `_run_diffusion("block")` with the literal, so it exercised
# a branch production never took and the suite stayed green. Guarded now in
# tests/test_dropped_upstream_guards.py::TestDiffusionUnification, all five validated
# to fail against the pre-fix source.
#
# The schemas.py half is worth its own note: `VLMRequest` is a `FlexibleBaseModel`
# (`extra="allow"`), so the 13 undeclared knobs still reached GenerationArguments and
# upstream's own test passes either way. What was lost is type/enum validation and
# OpenAPI visibility — `diffusion_sampler="nonsense"` and `block_length="abc"` were
# forwarded into the generation path instead of returning 422.

